    "details": "The RusTLS project reports:\n\n> functions retained a reference to the caller\\'s server_name buffer\n> after returning, rather than copying it. The API documentation did not\n> require the buffer to outlive the call and as a result if the caller\n> freed or reused the buffer, later TLS processing read freed memory.\n> \\[GHSA-rc3f-4j82-cmrg\\]\n",
